    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d616">

                <pb facs="0748" n="649" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg649"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">352.3515/1: Circular telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to All American Consular
                        Officers in Spain</hi><anchor n="70" xml:id="d616-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-07-29T17:00:00-04:00">July 29, 1936—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>At the request of the several governments you are authorized to extend insofar as
                    the circumstances permit your facilities for protection <pb facs="0749" n="650"
                        xml:id="pg650"/> and if necessary evacuation to the nationals of Argentina,
                    Austria, Belgium, Chile, Cuba, Finland, Panama, Sweden and Turkey.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d616-f1" n="70" type="source" xml:id="d616-f1-content">
                <p>Sent also to the Embassy at Madrid as telegram No. 56, July 29, 5 p.m.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
